{"link":{"rel":"self","url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/67b8b168d34e1a2e835b7e6c"},"relatedItems":{"link":{"url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/itemLinks?itemId=67b8b168d34e1a2e835b7e6c","rel":"related"}},"id":"67b8b168d34e1a2e835b7e6c","identifiers":[{"type":"DOI","scheme":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/vocab/category/item/identifier","key":"doi:10.5066/P1HTTCWN"}],"title":"World minerals outlook to 2029—Cobalt, gallium, helium, lithium, magnesium, palladium, platinum, and titanium data","summary":"Given the rapid expansion in the demand for mineral commodities that underpin worldwide economic growth and technological advancement, information regarding expected country-level mine production and production capacity is becoming increasingly important. In particular, production capacity can limit future supply, depending on how rapidly that capacity is able to expand. This World Minerals Outlook data release provides estimated capacities for cobalt, gallium, helium, lithium, magnesium, palladium, platinum, and titanium for 2024 through 2029. Production data from 2018 to 2024 are also provided and show the current and historical capacity utilization levels for these commodities.","body":"Given the rapid expansion in the demand for mineral commodities that underpin worldwide economic growth and technological advancement, information regarding expected country-level mine production and production capacity is becoming increasingly important. In particular, production capacity can limit future supply, depending on how rapidly that capacity is able to expand. This World Minerals Outlook data release provides estimated capacities for cobalt, gallium, helium, lithium, magnesium, palladium, platinum, and titanium for 2024 through 2029. Production data from 2018 to 2024 are also provided and show the current and historical capacity utilization levels for these commodities.","citation":"Alonso, E., Brioche, A.S., Schulte, R.F., Trimmer, L.M., Kim, J., Gulley, A.L., and Pineault, D.G., 2025, World minerals outlook to 2029—Cobalt, gallium, helium, lithium, magnesium, palladium, platinum, and titanium data: U.S. Geological Survey data release, https://doi.org/10.5066/P1HTTCWN.","purpose":"This data release represents production capacity data synthesized from government, industry, and company reports available as of June 2024 on near-term production, expansion, development, and closure for select metallic and non-metallic mineral commodities globally. The growing need for the important minerals that support economic growth and technology makes understanding mine production and capacity more essential. How much a mine can produce affects future supply, especially as capacities can change over time. This World Minerals Outlook data release provides the supply side data of the listed mineral commodities with current and historical production data, current country production capacity levels, and future production capacity outlook.","rights":"This work is marked with Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). ","provenance":{"dateCreated":"2025-02-21T17:01:28Z","lastUpdated":"2025-03-17T16:58:06Z"},"maintenanceUpdateFrequency":"None planned","hasChildren":false,"parentId":"5c8c03e4e4b0938824529f7d","contacts":[{"name":"Director, National Minerals Information Center","type":"Point of Contact","contactType":"person","email":"nmicrecordsmgt@usgs.gov","jobTitle":"Director","organization":{"displayText":"U.S. Geological Survey"},"primaryLocation":{"officePhone":"N/A","streetAddress":{},"mailAddress":{"line1":"12201 Sunrise Valley Dr. MS988","city":"Reston","state":"VA","zip":"20192","country":"United States of America"}}},{"name":"Elisa Alonso","oldPartyId":79943,"type":"Originator","contactType":"person","email":"ealonso@usgs.gov","active":true,"jobTitle":"Physical Scientist","firstName":"Elisa","lastName":"Alonso","organization":{},"primaryLocation":{"officePhone":"7036484990","streetAd